            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks, that is really helpful.\n\nI am beginning to think that *maybe* trying to predict if the file action will succeed before issuing a `willXxx` method would be easier and/or more robust than trying to revert bad action. I.e. the overall amount of bad cases for file action prediction (the prediction doesn't match the outcome) will be smaller than the overall amount of bad behaving LSP servers (which don't allow to \"revert\" the action). Hmm... Hard to tell.",
